Two high-cost risks are emerging beyond the six supplied claims: the contract’s synchronous “returns an outcome map” shape does not explain how browser/CLJD `attach!` can await a network handshake, and the end-to-end phase appears to require a stream-to-socket forwarding interpreter that the plan never names. I’m checking the legacy host implementations and build matrix now to separate genuine platform constraints from speculation.
