test/README.md:7:clj -M:cljd test            # all namespaces (sweeps the classpath)
test/README.md:8:clj -M:cljd test some.ns    # a subset
test/README.md:10:The native `cljd.build` test command compiles every `.cljc`/`.cljd` namespace on the classpath, generates a `*_test.dart` entrypoint under `test/cljd-out/` for each namespace containing deftests, and runs them via `flutter test`. There is no allowlist: JVM-only namespaces are excluded at the reader level with `#?(:cljd nil :clj ...)` guards (a plain `#?(:clj ...)` does NOT exclude code from the ClojureDart build, because the host pass also matches `:clj`).
test/README.md:20:./bin/run-cljs-tests.sh
test/README.md:22:This script uses `shadow-cljs` to compile the `:test` build and runs the resulting script with `node`.
test/README.md:25:The configuration for the test build is defined in `shadow-cljs.edn` under the `:test` key.
